(begin-tx "TX-LPG-04 - the HOMOGENEOUS ladder: does the second coil fit the user's scores?")
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 200000000)(env-gas 0)
(print "")
(print "=== TX-LPG-04 — HOMOGENEOUS ladder, per-score branching =======================")
;;==== TX-LPG-04 - homogeneous ladder · 01 · flip the lane to HOMOGENEOUS ==== ====================
(print "--- [TX-LPG-04 - homogeneous ladder · 01 · flip the lane to HOMOGENEOUS] ---")
;;WHY FLIP AN EXISTING LANE INSTEAD OF BUILDING A NEW FVT. The two modes route completely
;;differently and the DANGEROUS one is HOMOGENEOUS: there, bronze -> token-0, silver -> token-1
;;(one coil) and golden -> token-2 (TWO coils), so "how much to coil on the second hop" is decided
;;by WHICH scores the holder actually has. HETEROGENEOUS splits every lane across all three tokens
;;per the per-mille matrix, which MASKS that branching entirely -- a holder with no golden score
;;still receives token-2. So the heterogeneous assertions above, and every number measured on the
;;Custodians vault, say nothing about the per-score logic.
;;
;;OuroLpFarm is the tree's only homogeneous MULTIPLET lane, and post-boot it reads
;;lanes={lane-b 0, lane-s 0, lane-g 0, w-user 0} -- no staked weight, so claimable is 0 whatever is
;;injected. [6.4]_AQP-TRIPLET-COLLECT does reach it with a SILVER-ONLY profile (deb 110 on silver),
;;which proves the second coil is correctly SKIPPED. What that cannot reach is a GOLDEN lane, where
;;the second coil actually fires. The Custodians triplet has real weight on all three legs, and
;;`mode` is a parameter of C_SetQualitySplit -- so flipping it is the cheapest honest fixture.
(let
    (
        (patron:string KST.ANHD)
        (ouro-id:string "OURO-98c486052a51")
        (fvt-id:string (U|DALOS.UDC_Makeid "CustodiansVault"))
    )
    (env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
    (print (format "<(C_SetQualitySplit -> HOMOGENEOUS)> => \"{}\""
        [(TS02-C3.AQP-FVT|C_SetQualitySplit patron (AQP-FVT.UR_FVT|OwnerKonto fvt-id) fvt-id ouro-id
            "HOMOGENEOUS" [200 400 400] [400 300 300] [600 200 200])]))
    (print (format "ZZZ mode now = {}" [(RPS.UR_FVT-QS|Mode fvt-id ouro-id)]))
    (print (format "<(CC_Inject 3000 OURO)> => \"{}\""
        [(TS02-C3.AQP-FVT|CC_Inject patron patron fvt-id ouro-id 3000.0)]))
)
(env-sigs [])
(commit-tx)

